<speak>That's helpful. I sometimes leave the computer open because I think I might need it again, then forget it's there. I'll finish whatever I'm reading, sign out, and close it rather than leaving a row of pages open all evening. For my own notes, I'll write the portal question at the top of a fresh page. That way I won't bury it among the renovation reminders. I think the separate folders will make a difference, provided I actually use them rather than simply buying more stationery.</speak>